#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# denominator

#% text
# `denominator(x)` gives the denominator of a rational number, or the product of the factors of `x` with negative exponents, inverted.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# An integer has denominator 1. Sums are not combined over a common denominator.

#% item
# `denominator` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
denominator(6/15)
#% output
#= 5

#% cell
denominator(7)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
denominator(x^2/(y*z))
#% output
#= y*z

#% cell
denominator((x + 1)/(x - 1)^2)
#% output
#= (-1 + x)^2

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Each element of a list:

#% cell
denominator([1/2, 2/3, 3/4])
#% output
#= [2, 3, 4]

#% text
# Combine a sum first:

#% cell
denominator(together(1/x + 1/y))
#% output
#= x*y

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The least common denominator of several fractions:

#% cell
apply(lcm, denominator([1/6, 3/8, 5/12]))
#% output
#= 24

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `numerator`, `together`, `lcm`
